            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "rMZp7",
              "name": "ToggleSwitch Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": "$spacing-lg",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "J7NYO",
                  "name": "Docs Title",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-header",
                  "content": "ToggleSwitch",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "RS9uv",
                  "name": "Docs Subtitle",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-meta",
                  "content": "Toggle Input Atom",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "V0nWMB",
                  "name": "Purpose",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Purpose\nBinary on/off switch for toggling a single setting or feature. Provides immediate visual feedback of the current state. Use for enabling or disabling preferences, features, or modes.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "T3OJB",
                  "name": "When to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When to use\n• Toggling a binary setting (on/off, enable/disable)\n• Feature flags or preference switches\n• Immediate-effect controls that don't need a submit button\n• Settings pages, notification preferences, privacy controls",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "HEAIG",
                  "name": "When not",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When NOT to use\n• Multiple-choice selection (use Checkbox or Radio)\n• Actions that require confirmation (use Button)\n• Tri-state values (use Checkbox with indeterminate)\n• Form fields that are submitted together (use Checkbox)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "JRXOF",
                  "name": "Variants",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Variants & defaults\n• state: off · on · disabled · loading (default: off)\n\nThe base component represents the off state. On state moves the thumb to the right and changes the track color. Disabled reduces opacity. Loading replaces the toggle with a spinner.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "AeIB7",
                  "name": "Tokens",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Token usage\n• Container: 72 × 36 px, cornerRadius $radius-full (pill), padding $spacing-3xs (4 px)\n• Track off: $taupe-200 fill\n• Track on: $blue-100 fill\n• Thumb: 28 × 28 ellipse, $base-white fill, shadow-md\n• Thumb off fill: $base-white\n• Thumb on fill: $blue-600\n• Disabled: $taupe-200 with opacity 50%\n• Spinner track: $gray-100 ring, innerRadius 0.82\n• Spinner fill: $blue-600 arc (270°)\n• Spinner size: 32 × 32 px\n• Thumb transition: $duration-base + $easing-standard",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "r6Kyk",
                  "name": "A11y",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Accessibility\nToggleSwitch must expose a clear accessible label via aria-label. It must support keyboard interaction: Space key toggles the state. The element must have role=\"button\" and tabIndex=0. Loading state should announce loading status via role=\"status\" and sr-only text.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
