            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "b73sUM",
              "name": "PaginationDot Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": "$spacing-lg",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "CNd6T",
                  "name": "Title",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-header",
                  "content": "PaginationDot",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "q3guR",
                  "name": "Subtitle",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-meta",
                  "content": "Pagination Indicator Atom",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "jaINK",
                  "name": "Purpose",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Purpose\nA small circular pagination indicator dot used to show the current item or slide position. Used inside Carousel pagination rows, media position indicators, and compact item counters.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "V7mlR",
                  "name": "When to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When to use\n• Carousel pagination to indicate current slide\n• Media galleries to show position in a set\n• Compact item position indicators where numbered labels are too heavy\n• Any context showing position within a small ordered set (3–8 items)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "yaxR5",
                  "name": "When not",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When NOT to use\n• Navigation between pages (use TabItem or links)\n• Progress indicators (use Steps)\n• Large sets of items (use numbered pagination)\n• Toggle or selection controls (use Radio or SegmentItem)\n• Status badges or notification counts (use Badge or Tag)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "vPsK7",
                  "name": "Variants",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Variants & defaults\n• state: inactive (default) · active · disabled\n• size: 8×8 px (md, only size)\n\n3 component variants:\n  PaginationDot · PaginationDot/active · PaginationDot/disabled\n\nInactive uses $colors-borders-light. Active uses $gray-700. Disabled uses $gray-200.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "n8TI4R",
                  "name": "Tokens",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Token usage\n• Size: 8×8 px fixed\n• Shape: ellipse (inherently circular)\n• Inactive fill: $colors-borders-light\n• Active fill: $gray-700\n• Disabled fill: $gray-200\n• No stroke on any variant\n• Row gap between dots: $spacing-2xs (set on parent Indicators frame)\n• No hardcoded colors, radius, or transitions\n• Dots are visual indicators only — interactive dot behavior is out of scope",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "xG7Uq",
                  "name": "Resize",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Resize behavior\nPaginationDot keeps its fixed 8×8 size and does not stretch when placed inside a parent layout. It should remain centered in its row. The parent Indicators frame handles centering and gap spacing. No hidden, detached, fixed-width, or floating layers.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "xovy2",
                  "name": "A11y",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Accessibility\nPaginationDot is visual-only at the atom level. When dots become interactive in Carousel, each dot should have an accessible label like \"Go to slide 2\" and the active dot should expose current/selected state via aria-current. The dot row should be a listbox or tablist with each dot as an option. Screen readers should announce slide position (e.g. \"Slide 2 of 5\").",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
