            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "Wmskc",
              "name": "Callout Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": "$spacing-lg",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "e2MaY",
                  "name": "Docs Title",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-header",
                  "content": "Callout",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "p6lUUZ",
                  "name": "Docs Subtitle",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-meta",
                  "content": "P2 Feedback / Notification Molecule",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "wdl0g",
                  "name": "Purpose",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Purpose\nAn inline feedback surface that communicates status, context, or guidance. Callout is a P2 molecule based on the existing dev Alert component. In dev, Callout is a thin alias of Alert where intent maps to alertType. Built from P1 primitives: TextContent for title and description, Button/secondary for the action CTA, and lucide IconButton for the close control.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "r7488",
                  "name": "When to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When to use\n• Provide contextual information alongside page content\n• Surface success, warning, or error feedback inline\n• Display system notices or general-purpose notes\n• Guide users with actionable tips inside a page flow\n• Show dismissible notices the user can close",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "suJ9O",
                  "name": "When not to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When NOT to use\n• Transient notifications that auto-dismiss (use Toast / Snackbar)\n• Global system banners pinned to the top of the viewport\n• Form-field-level validation messages (use inline error text)\n• Confirmation dialogs requiring user action (use Dialog)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "E7KoO",
                  "name": "Variants",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Variants / Defaults\nIntent: info (default) | neutral | success | warning | error\nContent: title + description (default) | title-only\nOptional: dismissible (default false) | action (default false)\n\nAlert / Callout relationship\nCallout is the design name for the dev Alert component. Intent maps directly to alertType. The filled bgVariant is the default visual style. Each intent uses a dedicated color palette — no new tokens are introduced. All spacing, color, and typography values come from existing tokens.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "q7boX",
                  "name": "Token usage",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Token usage\n• Layout: horizontal, gap = $spacing-xs (12 px), padding = $spacing-sm (16 px)\n• Corner radius = $radius-2xs (8 px)\n• Title: $typo-primary-base-semibold (16 px, 600)\n• Description: $typo-primary-base-regular (16 px, normal)\n• Icon: 40 × 40 — outer ellipse at 30 % opacity + inner SVG path\n• Info: bg $sky-50, border $sky-100, icon $sky-300, text $sky-600 / 700\n• Neutral: bg $gray-50, border $gray-100, icon #64748B, text $gray-600 / 700\n• Success: bg $green-50, border $green-100, icon $green-400, text $green-600 / 700\n• Warning: bg $orange-50, border $orange-100, icon $orange-400, text $orange-600 / 700\n• Error: bg $red-50, border $red-100, icon $red-400, text $red-600 / 700\n• Stroke: 1 px inside, intent border token\n• Close icon: lucide x, 20 × 20, intent accent color\n• CTA: Button/secondary at sm size ($spacing-2xs / $spacing-sm padding)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Ci0uU",
                  "name": "Accessibility",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Accessibility\nInformational and neutral callouts are static content — no special ARIA role required. Warning and error callouts should use role=\"alert\" or role=\"status\" for assistive technology. Dismissible callouts must provide a keyboard-accessible close button with aria-label. Action CTA buttons must have descriptive labels. Title-only variant uses vertical centering (alignItems center) to align the single line with the icon.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "m4C92e",
