            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "vAW9k",
              "name": "ImageBlock Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 32,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "xUo7c",
                  "name": "Docs Title",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-header",
                  "content": "ImageBlock",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "B43dq8",
                  "name": "Docs Subtitle",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-meta",
                  "content": "Figure-Style Image Molecule",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "zgjsg",
                  "name": "Purpose",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Purpose\nA figure-style image block that combines a media region with an optional visible caption and optional credit line. ImageBlock composes the Image atom with TextContent to create a self-contained visual unit suitable for articles, cards, galleries, and content-heavy layouts.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "IKqoR",
                  "name": "When to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When to use\n• Display a photograph, illustration, or diagram with visible context\n• Article or blog post inline images with captions\n• Product or portfolio media with descriptive text\n• Card hero images that need attribution or explanation\n• Any figure element that pairs media with a human-readable caption",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Afipy",
                  "name": "When not to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When NOT to use\n• Decorative background images without captions (use Image atom directly)\n• Avatars or profile photos (use Avatar component)\n• Icon-sized graphics (use IconFont)\n• Image carousels or galleries (compose multiple ImageBlocks in a layout)\n• Thumbnails in data tables (use Image atom at small size)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "jjtCz",
                  "name": "Variants",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Variants / Defaults\n• caption: false | true  →  true\n• credit: false | true  →  false\n• image state: default | loading | error  →  default\n• image ratio: 16:9 | 4:3 | 1:1  →  16:9\n• image fit: cover | contain  →  cover\n• alignment: left | center  →  left\n\nVariant naming:\n• /caption-credit — image + caption + credit line\n• /no-caption — image only, no text\n• /loading — skeleton loading state\n• /error — broken image error state\n• /centered — center-aligned caption text",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "JU5d4",
                  "name": "Token usage",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Token usage\n• Image corner radius = $spacing-xs (12 px) — inherited from Image atom\n• Gap image → caption = $spacing-2xs (8 px)\n• Caption font = TextContent defaults ($typo-primary-base-regular, $colors-text-body)\n• Credit font = $typo-primary-xs-regular (12 px), $colors-text-meta\n• Credit line height = 1.3333\n• Component width = 320 px (matches Image atom default)\n• Image height 16:9 = 180 px, 4:3 = 240 px, 1:1 = 320 px\n• Image fit: cover (default) or contain via Image fill mode override",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "JRIba",
                  "name": "Accessibility",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Accessibility\nImage alt text and caption are different. Alt text describes the image for assistive technologies and is not visible on screen. Caption provides visible supporting context for all users. In implementation, wrap ImageBlock in a <figure> element and use <figcaption> for the caption. Decorative images may use an empty alt attribute (alt=\"\"). Credit text should be part of the figcaption or placed in a separate element — screen readers will announce it in document flow.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "ksbYd",
                  "name": "Accessibility",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Caption and credit can remain visible when the image is loading or in error state, if the consuming implementation provides that content.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "k3SRw",
          "name": "ImageBlock Demo Examples Title",
          "fill": "$sem-text-header",
          "content": "ImageBlock — Demo Examples",
          "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
          "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
          "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "hE4aB",
          "name": "ImageBlock Demos Row",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 40,
          "children": [
