                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Dashed and dotted lines are built as repeated segment groups inside a clipped horizontal frame, not stroke dashPattern (which does not render visually in Pencil). Goal uses 8px rectangles with 4px gap for dashes. Benchmark uses 2px rectangles with 4px gap for dots. Limit uses a solid rectangle fill. The clipped frame holds enough segments to cover widths up to ~700px; overflow segments are hidden. The label text is customizable via instance overrides."
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
