                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "YK9Qd",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Composition",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "o5eOEK",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "AreaChart = Card + CardHeader/description (title + subtitle) + chartBody (vertical frame) containing chartRow (horizontal: yAxis labels + plotArea) and xAxis labels. PlotArea (layout: vertical, clip: true) has the area fill path as its flex child (gradient fill, no stroke) for responsive scaling. A separate line stroke path (open curve, stroke only) is absolutely positioned on top. Grid lines, activeDot, and ChartTooltip instance are also inside plotArea or chartRow. The reference line is a ThresholdLine/goal instance (dashed, $orange-500) placed absolutely inside plotArea with label override. The scrubber is a vertical dashed segment frame (2px wide, $colors-text-disabled, 6px segments / 4px gap, clipped) positioned absolutely in plotArea. ChartTooltip sits outside the clipped plotArea — it is a sibling in chartRow with layoutPosition: absolute, so it is never clipped."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "E14Uq",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Token usage",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "G0wA3p",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Card: $colors-background-surface, $colors-borders-light, $radius-sm. Area fill: gradient $chart-sequential/seq-300 to seq-100 at 50% opacity. Line stroke: $chart-sequential/seq-500, 2px (separate open-curve path). Selected dot: $chart-sequential/seq-500, 8px. Grid: $colors-borders-light. Axis line: $colors-borders-dark. Reference line: ThresholdLine/goal instance — dashed $orange-500, label overridden to chart-specific text. Scrubber: vertical dashed segments, $colors-text-disabled, 2px wide, 6px segments / 4px gap. Tick labels: $typo-primary-2xs-regular, $colors-text-meta. Header: CardHeader/description tokens. Tooltip: ChartTooltip component tokens."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "PIAFg",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Resize behavior",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "Dgw1Y",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Card fills available width via fill_container. chartBody, chartRow, and plotArea all use fill_container to propagate width. The area fill path is the flex child of plotArea (layout: vertical), so it scales with the container via fill_container width. Grid lines extend to 5000px and are clipped by plotArea. Y-axis labels stay aligned. X-axis labels distribute via space_between. ChartTooltip is outside the clipped plotArea (absolute positioned in chartRow) so it is never cut off. The ThresholdLine/goal reference line extends to 5000px and is clipped by plotArea, expanding naturally when the chart resizes. The dashed scrubber uses a clipped vertical segment frame — its fixed position is for the static design; implementation would position it dynamically."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "yQIwR",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Accessibility",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "e9OwW",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Chart needs accessible title and description. Provide a text summary of the data trend. Tooltip values should be available through keyboard/focus interaction. Do not rely on color alone — the series is identified by title/subtitle. Axis labels and values remain readable. Text contrast: $colors-text-header on $colors-background-surface exceeds 4.5:1. Chart line/area contrast: $chart-sequential/seq-500 against white exceeds 3:1."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "aTNm8",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Implementation note",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "LMPpy",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "This is a visual chart component. Real chart rendering, data binding, tooltip positioning, pointer events, keyboard interaction, responsive chart logic, and animation are implementation concerns. The visual component defines structure, token usage, states, and expected behavior."
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
