            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "Xcv87",
              "name": "WaterfallChart Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 32,
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "iDT0L",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "WaterfallChart",
                      "fontSize": "$text-size-lg",
                      "fontWeight": "700",
                      "lineHeight": 1.3333
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "Yy8cU",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "A waterfall chart organism showing how an initial value is affected by sequential positive and negative changes. Built on Card with CardHeader, y-axis labels, a clipped plot area with start/total bars, increment/decrement bars, and connecting lines between bars."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "F7zTxm",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "When to use",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "MHpcx",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Use for financial bridge analysis: starting balance through income, expenses, taxes, and growth to a final total. The waterfall format makes it easy to see which factors contributed most. Use with-positive-negative to color-code gains vs losses. Use compact in dense dashboards. Use no-card when embedding inside another container."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "BTs09",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "When not to use",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "T6rvs",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Do not use for simple comparisons between categories — use BarChart instead. Do not use for time-series trends — use AreaChart. Do not use when there are more than 8–10 waterfall steps — the chart becomes too crowded."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "jXX9A",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Variants",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "VS8K6",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "default: Standard waterfall with sequential/seq-500 start/total bars and categorical/color-01 increment bars.\nwith-positive-negative: Positive bars use $colors-text-deposit (green), negative bars use $colors-text-error (red) for clear gain/loss signaling. Value labels use MoneyText instances (default/positive/negative) with $typo-primary-2xs-regular overrides.\nwith-tooltip: Default with ChartTooltip/multi-series positioned near the selected step. Tooltip shows step change value and running total. Values use MoneyText instances (MoneyText/positive for gains). Marker color matches the selected bar color.\ncompact: 360px width, 140px plot height, 32px bar width.\nno-card: Same chart structure without Card wrapper, for embedding in other containers."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "z5e1d",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Composition",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "HBhk5",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "WaterfallChart = Card + CardHeader/description + chartBody (chartRow: yAxis + plotArea) + xAxis + valuesRow + optional ChartTooltip. PlotArea (layout: none, clip: true) contains grid lines, start/total bars, increment/decrement bars with cornerRadius [2,2,0,0] or [0,0,2,2] for negative. Connector lines (1px $colors-borders-light rectangles) link bar tops between steps. ValuesRow uses MoneyText component instances in the with-positive-negative variant. With-tooltip adds ChartTooltip/multi-series (layoutPosition: absolute) inside chartBody, positioned near the selected step bar."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "K8wTY",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Token usage",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "QkisC",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Start/Total bars: $chart-sequential/seq-500, cornerRadius [2,2,0,0]. Positive bars: $colors-text-deposit (with-positive-negative) or $chart-categorical/color-01 (default). Negative bars: $colors-text-error (with-positive-negative) or $chart-categorical/color-01 (default), cornerRadius [0,0,2,2]. Connectors: $colors-borders-light, 1px height. Grid: $colors-borders-light. Axis: $colors-borders-dark. Labels: $typo-primary-2xs-regular, $colors-text-meta. Value labels (with-positive-negative): MoneyText instances with $typo-primary-2xs-regular overrides. Tooltip (with-tooltip): ChartTooltip tokens — $colors-background-surface fill, $colors-borders-light stroke, outer shadow. Tooltip values use MoneyText (positive variant for gains)."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "QQ0FT",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Resize behavior",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "UkWCp",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Card fills available width. Grid lines extend to 5000px and clip. Bar positions are absolute within the plot area — positions should be recalculated when container width changes. Y-axis labels stay aligned. X-axis labels distribute via space_between."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "TIaIb",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Accessibility",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "PgBdY",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Bars should meet 3:1 non-text contrast against background. Provide text summary of the waterfall data. In with-positive-negative, do not rely on color alone — use labels or patterns to distinguish positive from negative. Axis labels remain readable."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "Ztt2k",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Implementation note",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "H0Mk1k",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "This is a visual chart component. Real bar positioning, data binding, connector line calculation, hover states, tooltip on bar interaction, and animation are implementation concerns."
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
