            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "HweSf",
              "name": "HeatmapChart Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 32,
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "YfRcD",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "HeatmapChart",
                      "fontSize": "$text-size-lg",
                      "fontWeight": "700",
                      "lineHeight": 1.3333
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "NpJrb",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "A heatmap chart organism displaying a matrix of values using color intensity. Built on Card with CardHeader, y-axis row labels, and a grid of cells whose fill color represents data magnitude. Supports sequential (single-color) and diverging (positive/negative) color scales."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "DgnK0",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "When to use",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "QRebO",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Use for correlation matrices, asset class return grids, or any 2D data where magnitude is encoded by color. Use positive-negative when values range from negative to positive. Use with-labels to add descriptive text per cell and a gradient scale legend. Use compact in dense dashboards."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "tqu6d",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "When not to use",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "bz7A3",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Do not use for small datasets — a simple table is clearer. Do not use when exact values matter more than relative magnitude — a data table is better. Do not use for time-series data — use AreaChart or line charts."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "seHWZ",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Variants",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "HZvjF",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "default: Sequential intensity using $chart-sequential/seq-100 to seq-600. Cell text ink is chosen by the cell fill, not by theme: $colors-text-reverse on cells that flip with the theme, $gray-900 on mid-range fills that stay blue in both themes.\npositive-negative: Green cells ($green-100 to $green-600) for positive, red ($red-200) for negative.\ncompact: 360px width with smaller cells.\nwith-labels: Adds descriptive labels (Strong/Moderate/Mild/Weak) per cell at full opacity, using the same per-cell ink rule as the default variant. Includes a gradient scale bar (Low→High)."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "iJAkJ",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Composition",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "e6cWvG",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "HeatmapChart = Card + CardHeader/description + chartBody (y-axis labels + cellGrid rows). CellGrid is vertical with horizontal rows. Each cell is a fill_container frame with centered text. With-labels adds a gradient scale bar row below the grid (linear gradient from seq-100 to seq-700, rotation: 270)."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "B7gj6J",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Token usage",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "F9Vr5",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Sequential cells: $chart-sequential/seq-100 (low) to seq-600 (high); in dark mode the ramp is inverted, so seq-100 is the darkest step. Positive cells: $green-100 to $green-600. Negative cells: $red-200. Cell text: $colors-text-reverse on theme-flipping cells, $gray-900 on mid-range cells, $colors-text-header on seq-100/seq-200. Every pairing clears 4.5:1 in both themes. Row labels: $typo-primary-2xs-regular, $colors-text-meta. Header: CardHeader/description tokens. Gradient bar: linear gradient seq-100→seq-700."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "GarU7",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Resize behavior",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "jgY8S",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Card fills available width. Cells use fill_container to distribute evenly within rows. Cell grid rows use fill_container width. Y-axis labels have fixed width. The gradient scale bar stretches with fill_container."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "B6Dkg",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Accessibility",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "FtC6w",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Text contrast must meet WCAG 4.5:1. Dark cells use $colors-text-reverse (white text), light cells use $colors-text-header (dark text). Descriptive labels in with-labels use full-opacity text tokens — no opacity reduction. Do not rely on color alone — with-labels variant adds text descriptions. Provide accessible summary of the data. For positive-negative, color meaning should be described in legend or context."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "bdzgE",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Implementation note",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "kaoHX",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "This is a visual chart component. Real data binding, color scale calculation, hover states, tooltip on cell interaction, responsive cell sizing, and animation are implementation concerns."
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
