            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "p8qFf",
              "name": "BenchmarkComparisonChart Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 32,
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "WTHgq",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "BenchmarkComparisonChart",
                      "fontSize": "$text-size-lg",
                      "fontWeight": "700",
                      "lineHeight": 1.3333
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "SuUPg",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "A benchmark comparison chart organism showing portfolio returns vs index/benchmark performance side by side. Built on Card with CardHeader, grouped bars (2 per category), y-axis labels, x-axis category labels, and an inline legend. Each bar group compares Portfolio (color-01) against Benchmark (color-02)."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "mIoBb",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "When to use",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "SehJY",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Use for comparing portfolio/fund returns against a benchmark index across asset classes or time periods. The grouped bar format makes direct comparison easy. Use with-labels to show exact percentage values above bars. Use compact in dense dashboards. Use no-card when embedding inside another container."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "ySUIP",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "When not to use",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "DqSIq",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Do not use for time-series trends — use ProjectedVsActualChart or AreaChart. Do not use for a single series — use a simple BarChart. Do not use with more than 6–7 categories — the bars become too crowded."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "CmRYI",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Variants",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "ydxi2",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "default: Grouped bars with Portfolio (color-01) and Benchmark (color-02) per category.\nwith-labels: Same as default plus percentage value labels above each bar.\nwith-tooltip: Default with ChartTooltip/with-total positioned near the selected category. Shows Portfolio and Benchmark percentage values in value rows. Difference in the total row using positive/negative semantic styling. Markers match bar series colors.\ncompact: 360px width, 140px plot height, 14px bar width.\nno-card: Same chart structure without Card wrapper."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "NRmd5",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Composition",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "xsraW",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "BenchmarkComparisonChart = Card + CardHeader/description + chartBody (chartRow: yAxis + plotArea) + xAxis + legendRow + optional ChartTooltip. PlotArea (layout: none, clip: true) contains grid lines and barGroup frames. Each barGroup is a horizontal flex frame (alignItems: end, gap: 3–4) with two bars. With-labels wraps each bar in a vertical frame with a text label above. Legend row has square color markers + text labels. With-tooltip adds ChartTooltip/with-total (layoutPosition: absolute) inside chartBody showing portfolio/benchmark values and their difference for the selected category."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "g2Xu2j",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Token usage",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "En60F",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Portfolio bars: $chart-categorical/color-01, cornerRadius [2,2,0,0]. Benchmark bars: $chart-categorical/color-02, cornerRadius [2,2,0,0]. Bar width: 20px (default), 14px (compact). Legend markers: 8px squares, cornerRadius 2. Grid: $colors-borders-light. Axis: $colors-borders-dark. Labels: $typo-primary-2xs-regular, $colors-text-meta. Value labels: 9px, $colors-text-meta, fontWeight 600. Legend text: $typo-primary-sm-regular, $colors-text-body. Tooltip (with-tooltip): ChartTooltip tokens — $colors-background-surface fill, $colors-borders-light stroke, outer shadow. Difference uses positive/negative semantic token styling."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "ZCAVZ",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Resize behavior",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a9aEWY",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Card fills available width. Grid lines extend to 5000px and clip. Bar groups are absolutely positioned — positions should be recalculated when container width changes. Y-axis labels stay aligned. X-axis labels distribute via space_between. Bar width remains fixed regardless of container width."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "eC1E4",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Accessibility",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "npaA7",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Legend is required — it maps colors to Portfolio/Benchmark labels. Do not rely on color alone. Bar colors ($chart-categorical/color-01 and color-02) meet 3:1 non-text contrast against background. With-labels variant provides exact values. Provide text summary of performance comparison. Axis labels remain readable."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "o1pTFh",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Implementation note",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "iauHQ",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "This is a visual chart component. Real bar positioning, data binding, hover states, tooltip on bar interaction, responsive bar redistribution, and animation are implementation concerns."
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
