            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "grIZQ",
              "name": "DualAxisChart Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 32,
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "j3MoP",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "DualAxisChart",
                      "fontSize": "$text-size-lg",
                      "fontWeight": "700",
                      "lineHeight": 1.3333
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "R8M3Z3",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "A dual-axis chart organism displaying two data series with independent left and right Y-axes. The primary series renders as a solid line, the secondary series as a dotted line. Built on Card with CardHeader/description and inline ChartLegend."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "b4oqyf",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "When to use",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "MSdpi",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Use when comparing two metrics with different scales on the same time axis — e.g. portfolio value ($) vs confidence score (0–100). Use with-events when key dates need marking. Use compact in dense dashboards. Use no-card when embedding inside another container."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "VZN7p",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "When not to use",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "pYt1q",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Do not use for metrics with the same scale — use AreaChartMultiSeries instead. Do not use for more than two series — dual axes become confusing. Do not use for categorical data — use BarChart."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "x8sRzv",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Variants",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "hnUOQ",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "default: Card wrapper with CardHeader/description, inline legend (2 items), solid primary line (left Y-axis), dotted secondary line (right Y-axis).\nwith-events: Same as default plus dashed vertical event markers with labels (Exercise, Sale) at specific positions.\nwith-tooltip: Same as default plus a vertical selection line at a chosen point, selection dots for both series, and a ChartTooltip/multi-series overlay showing exact values — monetary value uses MoneyText, score value uses plain text.\ncompact: 360px width, 150px plot height, CardHeader title-only, fewer axis ticks, smaller legend dots.\nno-card: CardHeader + legend + chart without Card wrapper, for embedding in other containers."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "O73yug",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Composition",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "UZ90Q",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "DualAxisChart = Card + CardHeader/description + legendRow (inline legend items) + chartBody (chartRow with yAxisLeft + plotArea + yAxisRight, xAxis). PlotArea contains grid lines, axis line, primary solid line path, and secondary dotted line (repeated small ellipses along the curve). Left/right Y-axes use their respective series colors. With-tooltip adds a selection line, two selection dots, and a ChartTooltip/multi-series overlay to chartContent."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a0Vzd",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Token usage",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "FMfhD",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Primary line: $chart-categorical/color-01 (solid stroke). Secondary dots: $chart-categorical/color-02. Left Y-axis labels: color-01. Right Y-axis labels: $colors-text-meta. X-axis labels: $colors-text-meta. Event markers: color-04 (Exercise), color-02 (Sale). Legend markers match series colors. Grid: $colors-borders-light. Axis: $colors-borders-dark. Labels: $typo-primary-2xs-regular. Tooltip uses ChartTooltip tokens — monetary value ($195K) uses MoneyText, score value (75) uses plain text. Tooltip marker colors match series: color-01 (Portfolio Value), color-02 (Confidence Score), color-04 (Event)."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "e7zVlX",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Resize behavior",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "R2aI2",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Card fills available width. PlotArea uses fill_container width. Left and right Y-axes have fixed widths (40px and 28px). The primary line path scales with fill_container. Secondary dots are absolutely positioned in the plotArea. Compact variant reduces plot height to 150px and axis tick count."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "a3Voz",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Accessibility",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "DqDJP",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Both series are distinguished by line style (solid vs dotted) AND color AND legend labels — color is never the sole identifier. Y-axis labels use their series color on $colors-background-surface for context. Event markers use dashed lines AND text labels. All text meets WCAG AA contrast on the surface background."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "W1nC9",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Implementation note",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "C51cN",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "The secondary dotted line uses repeated 4×4 ellipses absolutely positioned along the curve, since Pencil's stroke dashPattern does not render on path geometry. The with-tooltip variant uses a ChartTooltip/multi-series instance positioned absolutely over the chart area. Dynamic data binding, hover/crosshair interaction, tooltip display, and axis scaling are implementation concerns."
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
