            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "B5nXl",
              "name": "MoneyText Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": "$spacing-lg",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Jpb8w",
                  "name": "Docs Title",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-header",
                  "content": "MoneyText",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "B8JFvI",
                  "name": "Docs Subtitle",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-meta",
                  "content": "Financial Amount Atom",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "xFnCi",
                  "name": "Purpose",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Purpose\nA single text atom for displaying monetary amounts. MoneyText renders a formatted currency value with appropriate tone coloring (positive, negative, muted) and right-alignment for numeric column readability.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "ncTcn",
                  "name": "When to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When to use\n• Transaction amounts in tables, lists, and detail views\n• Account balances and portfolio values\n• Gain/loss indicators on holdings and performance cards\n• Any formatted currency value that needs tone context",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "KkTjQ",
                  "name": "When not",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When NOT to use\n• Non-monetary numbers (percentages, counts, IDs) — use plain text\n• Editable amount inputs — use Input\n• Full transaction rows or cards — compose with MoneyText inside a layout\n• Currency conversion labels — use a custom text pattern",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "V0Jj9V",
                  "name": "Variants",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Variants & defaults\n• tone: default (default) · positive · negative · muted\n• size: sm · md (default) · lg\n• align: left · right (default)\n\n6 component variants:\n  MoneyText · MoneyText/positive · MoneyText/negative · MoneyText/muted · MoneyText/sm · MoneyText/lg\n\nAlignment is controlled via textAlign override on instances.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Z2pY5b",
                  "name": "Tokens",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Token usage\n• sm: typo-primary-sm-semibold (Heebo 14/20/600)\n• md: typo-primary-base-semibold (Heebo 16/24/600)\n• lg: typo-primary-xl-semibold (Heebo 24/32/600)\n• default tone: $colors-text-header\n• positive tone: $colors-text-deposit\n• negative tone: $colors-text-error\n• muted tone: $colors-text-meta\n• fontWeight hardcoded as \"600\" (number-typed tokens incompatible with fontWeight)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "T1UZLM",
                  "name": "A11y",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Accessibility\nMoneyText preserves the sign character and currency symbol in plain text so screen readers can interpret the full amount. Negative values use a real minus sign (−), not a hyphen. Avoid visually hiding the sign or relying solely on color to convey positive/negative meaning — always pair color with a text indicator (+, −, or contextual label).",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
