                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "QgBQU",
              "name": "Collapse Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 32,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Snycz",
                  "name": "Docs Title",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-header",
                  "content": "Collapse",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "nO7P2",
                  "name": "Docs Subtitle",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-meta",
                  "content": "Expandable Section Primitive",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "lRLKc",
                  "name": "Purpose",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Purpose\nA disclosure primitive that toggles visibility of a content region. Collapse provides a trigger row with a title and chevron indicator, plus a collapsible content area below. It implements the HeadlessUI Disclosure pattern — click the trigger to expand or collapse the content. Supports an alwaysExpanded mode where the chevron is hidden and content remains visible.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "yMbMt",
                  "name": "When to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When to use\n• Hide secondary details until the user requests them\n• FAQ sections or help panels\n• Settings groups that can be collapsed\n• Long content pages where sections can be minimized\n• Building blocks for Accordion components",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "vuNAD",
                  "name": "When not to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When NOT to use\n• Tabbed navigation between views (use TabsGroup)\n• Modal or dialog content (use Dialog)\n• Tooltip-style hover reveals (use Tooltip)\n• Content that must always be visible (use a Stack or Card)\n• Stepper or wizard flows (use Steps)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "eWA39",
                  "name": "Variants",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Variants / Defaults\n• state: closed | open  →  closed\n\nThe closed variant shows only the trigger row with a downward chevron. The open variant shows the trigger with an upward chevron plus the content region below. No disabled variant — the source component does not support a disabled prop.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Kwayl",
                  "name": "Token usage",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Token usage\n• Title = $typo-primary-lg-regular, $colors-text-body\n• Chevron icon = lucide chevron-down, 20 × 20, $colors-text-body\n• Chevron rotation: closed = 0°, open = 180°\n• Trigger layout = horizontal, justify space-between, align center\n• Gap trigger → content = $spacing-xs (12 px)\n• Content = TextContent component ($typo-primary-base-regular, $colors-text-body)\n• Width = full width of parent (320 px default)\n• Open/close transition: $duration-base + $easing-standard",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "J4iwC",
                  "name": "Accessibility",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Accessibility\nThe trigger should be a button element and expose aria-expanded=\"true\" when open and aria-expanded=\"false\" when closed. The content region should have a unique ID referenced by the trigger's aria-controls. Keyboard users should be able to toggle with Enter or Space. When alwaysExpanded is true, the trigger should still reflect aria-expanded=\"true\" but may not need to be interactive.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
