            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "l0RVT",
              "name": "Card Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": "$spacing-lg",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "J2whNM",
                  "name": "Docs Title",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-header",
                  "content": "Card",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "ucYIr",
                  "name": "Docs Subtitle",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-meta",
                  "content": "Presentational Surface Molecule",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Kriow",
                  "name": "Purpose",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Purpose\nA presentational surface for grouped content. Card provides background, border, radius, and optional shadow — creating a visually bounded region that separates one group of information from another. Internal content layout is delegated to an embedded Stack primitive, which handles vertical spacing, gap, and child alignment. Card owns the surface; Stack owns the layout.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "yzbzE",
                  "name": "When to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When to use\n• Group related content with a visible boundary\n• Create visual separation between content sections\n• Contain form fields, settings, or profile information\n• Hold summary or metric blocks on dashboards\n• Wrap preview content (articles, products, media)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "y09qw",
                  "name": "When not to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When NOT to use\n• Full-width page sections without visual boundaries (use Stack)\n• Navigation containers (use Nav or Sidebar)\n• Interactive surfaces that respond to click/tap (use a button or link wrapper)\n• Modal or dialog containers (use Dialog)\n• Inline text grouping (use a span or paragraph)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "oDyQK",
                  "name": "Variants",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Variants / Defaults\n• padding: sm ($spacing-sm) | md ($spacing-md) | lg ($spacing-lg)  →  md\n• tone: default (surface) | subtle (light)  →  default\n• border: true | false  →  true\n• shadow: none | sm  →  none\n• density: default (sm Stack gap + sm padding) | dense (sm Stack gap + sm padding)  →  default\n\nCard does not define its own content gap — the internal Stack determines child spacing via its gap property.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "xCiw6",
                  "name": "Token usage",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Token usage\n• Background default = $colors-background-surface (white)\n• Background subtle = $colors-background-light (gray-50)\n• Border = $colors-borders-light (1 px inside)\n• Corner radius = $radius-sm (16 px)\n• Padding sm = $spacing-sm (16 px)\n• Padding md = $spacing-md (24 px)\n• Padding lg = $spacing-lg (32 px)\n• Stack gap default = $spacing-sm (16 px) — internal vertical spacing between content children\n• Stack gap lg = $spacing-md (24 px)\n• Shadow sm = $shadow-sm-* tokens (outer, y $shadow-sm-y, blur $shadow-sm-blur, color $shadow-sm-color)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "FcNgy",
                  "name": "Accessibility",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Accessibility\nCard is presentational by default and does not create landmark semantics. It renders as a plain container (div). Consuming implementations should add appropriate ARIA roles, landmarks, or headings only when the grouped content requires it — for example, role=\"region\" with an aria-label when the card represents a distinct section.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
