            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "I8Qi0r",
              "name": "Accordion Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 32,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "qPrOH",
                  "name": "Docs Title",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-header",
                  "content": "Accordion",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Mwrxn",
                  "name": "Docs Subtitle",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-meta",
                  "content": "Expandable Section Group Molecule",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "u9vc7",
                  "name": "Purpose",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Purpose\nA vertical group of Collapse primitives that forms an expandable/collapsible section list. Accordion arranges items in a stack, manages which items are open via mode (single or multiple), and delegates all trigger and content rendering to the Collapse atom. It is a purely structural and behavioral molecule — open/closed state management is handled by implementation.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "w6OLlP",
                  "name": "When to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When to use\n• Group related collapsible sections into an FAQ or settings panel\n• Show multiple sections where only one should be open at a time (single mode)\n• Allow users to expand multiple sections simultaneously (multiple mode)\n• Organize long-form content into scannable, titled sections\n• Build progressive disclosure patterns for complex forms or guides",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Uv8cl",
                  "name": "When not to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When NOT to use\n• Single collapsible section (use Collapse directly)\n• Tabbed navigation where content views switch in place (use TabsGroup)\n• Stepper or wizard flows with sequential steps (use Steps)\n• Sidebar or primary navigation (use Nav components)\n• Content that should always be visible (use Stack or Card)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "HkfJE",
                  "name": "Variants",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Variants / Defaults\n• itemCount: 2 | 3 | 4  →  3\n• openItem: none | first | middle | last  →  first\n• multipleOpen: false | true  →  false\n  (accordion.tsx supports mode='single' | 'multiple')\n\nVariant naming:\n• /2-items — two-item accordion\n• /4-items — four-item accordion\n• /mid-open — middle item expanded\n• /last-open — last item expanded\n• /all-closed — no items expanded\n• /multiple-open — first and last items expanded (mode='multiple')\n\nNote: accordion.tsx does not expose a disabled prop on AccordionItem, so no disabled variant exists.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "jxLpy",
                  "name": "Token usage",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Token usage\n• Layout = vertical (items stacked, no gap between items)\n• Width = 320 px (matches Collapse primitive width)\n• Each item = Collapse or Collapse/open instance at fill_container width\n• Closed item trigger row height = 56 px (override on Collapse trigger frame), vertically centered text and chevron\n• Open item trigger row height = 56 px (override on Collapse/open trigger frame)\n• Open item bottom padding = $spacing-md (creates space between content and the separator below)\n• Separator between each item = Separator primitive at fill_container width ($colors-borders-light, 1 px line, padding [0, 0] for full-width edge-to-edge dividers)\n• No separator after the last item\n• Trigger row = inherited from Collapse (typo-primary-lg-regular, $colors-text-body)\n• Chevron = inherited from Collapse (lucide chevron-down, 20×20, rotated 180° when open)\n• Content text = inherited from Collapse/open (TextContent ref, $spacing-xs gap from trigger)",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "TGafd",
                  "name": "Accessibility",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Accessibility\nAccordion should use accessible Collapse triggers with aria-expanded on each item's button. In single mode, opening one item closes all others. In multiple mode, each item toggles independently. Keyboard interaction should follow the disclosure/accordion pattern: Enter or Space to toggle the focused trigger, Tab to move between triggers, and aria-controls linking each trigger to its panel. The container should convey grouping semantics. AccordionItem does not support a disabled state in the current implementation.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
