            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "Te0ua",
              "name": "ModalDrawer Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 32,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "n9s7Fg",
                  "name": "Docs Title",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-header",
                  "content": "ModalDrawer",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "i3Oso",
                  "name": "Docs Subtitle",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-meta",
                  "content": "Slot-Based Overlay Shell",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "dxOLd",
                  "name": "Purpose",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Purpose\nA reusable slot-based overlay shell for modal or drawer content. ModalDrawer provides a dimmed backdrop, a centered surface panel, replaceable header/body/footer slots, and a close affordance. Product-specific detail drawers (AccountDetailDrawer, TransactionDetailDrawer, HoldingDetailDrawer) should inject their own content into these slots rather than embedding product-specific content directly.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "k3mXTY",
                  "name": "When to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When to use\n• Account detail drawer\n• Transaction detail drawer\n• Holding detail drawer\n• Focused overlay content that keeps the user in the current context\n• Forms, filters, or detail panels that need a modal/drawer shell\n• Settings or profile editing overlays",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "K26oR4",
                  "name": "When not to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When NOT to use\n• Simple confirmation dialog — use Dialog if available\n• Toast/snackbar notifications — use Callout or toast patterns\n• Inline expandable content — use Collapse or Accordion\n• Full navigation page — use routing or page-level navigation\n• Persistent sidebar navigation that remains open",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "bjJjX",
                  "name": "Variants",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Variants\n\ndefault\nDesktop content-only. Centered panel with headerSlot and bodySlot. footerSlot is present but disabled. No actions visible.\n\n/with-actions\nDesktop with footer actions. Same centered panel with headerSlot and bodySlot. footerSlot is enabled and contains a primary Button and an outline Button instance.\n\n/scroll\nDesktop scrollable body. Same centered panel with headerSlot. bodySlot has clip enabled so content scrolls internally. A scroll indicator (thin vertical bar) is absolutely positioned inside the bodySlot. Header remains fixed above the scrollable area. footerSlot is present but disabled.\n\n/mobile\nMobile bottom sheet. Panel anchored to the bottom of the viewport (justifyContent: end) with rounded top corners. headerSlot, bodySlot, and footerSlot (disabled) follow the same slot pattern. Panel width fills the mobile viewport (375 px).\n\nAll variants include headerSlot, bodySlot, and footerSlot. footerSlot is disabled by default in content-only variants and can be enabled via instance override.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "xeS6m",
                  "name": "Composition",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Composition\n\nModalDrawer (viewport frame, clip: true)\n  └ Backdrop — absolute-positioned rectangle, covers full viewport\n  └ Panel — centered surface, vertical layout\n      ├ Header — horizontal frame, center-aligned\n      │   ├ headerSlot — replaceable slot placeholder\n      │   └ Close Button — lucide x icon, 20 × 20\n      ├ bodySlot — replaceable content area\n      └ footerSlot — optional actions area (disabled by default)\n\nToken usage\n• Backdrop: $gray-900 at 50% opacity\n• Surface: $colors-background-surface\n• Corner radius: $radius-sm\n• Shadow: $shadow-overlay-y, $shadow-overlay-blur, $shadow-overlay-color\n\nDesktop layout\n• Root: 960 × 640, padding [$spacing-xl, 0], justifyContent center, alignItems center\n• Panel: 560 × 480\n• Header: padding [$spacing-xl, $spacing-lg, 0, $spacing-xl], gap $spacing-sm\n• bodySlot: padding $spacing-xl, fill_container height\n\nMobile layout\n• Root: 375 × 812, padding [$spacing-xl, 0, 0, 0], justifyContent end\n• Panel: 375 × 480, cornerRadius [$radius-sm, $radius-sm, 0, 0]\n• Header: padding [$spacing-md, $spacing-xs, 0, $spacing-sm], gap $spacing-sm\n• bodySlot: padding $spacing-sm, gap 16\n\nSlot convention\n• headerSlot — replace with DetailHeader (logo/avatar + title)\n• bodySlot — replace with DetailSection, AccountRowGroup, TransactionTable, etc.\n• footerSlot — enable and populate with Button instances when actions needed\n\nResize behavior\n• Desktop: panel centered via flex. Backdrop fills via fill_container + absolute position.\n• Mobile: panel anchored to bottom via justifyContent: end. Top corners rounded, bottom flush.\n• bodySlot: fills remaining panel height. Scroll variant clips overflow.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "iIdNj",
                  "name": "Accessibility",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Accessibility\n• Focus trap — trap focus while open, cycling between interactive elements within the panel\n• Escape closes — Escape key must close the drawer\n• aria-modal — panel should have role=\"dialog\" and aria-modal=\"true\", with title linked via aria-labelledby\n• Return focus to trigger — focus returns to the triggering element after close\n• Background inert — content behind the overlay should be marked inert or aria-hidden to prevent assistive technology interaction\n• Close button — must have aria-label=\"Close drawer\"\n• Scrollable body — in the /scroll variant, the scrollable region must remain keyboard accessible\n\nImplementation note\nModalDrawer is a generic shell. Product-specific drawer components should replace the slot placeholders with real content:\n• headerSlot — custom header with logo, avatar, title, subtitle, balance, etc.\n• bodySlot — detail content, forms, data rows, section blocks, lists, tables\n• footerSlot — action buttons (submit/cancel), links, or other footer content\n\nAccountDetailDrawer, TransactionDetailDrawer, and HoldingDetailDrawer should be built as separate components on top of this ModalDrawer shell. Do not embed product-specific content directly into the base ModalDrawer component.\n\nFooter/actions are optional and should be included only when the flow requires explicit user actions (confirm, cancel, submit, etc.).",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
