            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "ePyRz",
              "name": "ListRow Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 32,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "JaCRH",
                  "name": "Docs Title",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-header",
                  "content": "ListRow",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "U4wk6",
                  "name": "Docs Subtitle",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-meta",
                  "content": "Interactive List Row Molecule",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "X97jyf",
                  "name": "Purpose",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Purpose\nA reusable row molecule for list items inside generated UI blocks. ListRow has two modes: chevron variants for interactive/clickable rows that open detail views or trigger actions, and no-chevron variants for informational rows that display data without interaction. It is designed for use inside P3 organisms like ListBlock, SectionBlock, and Card-based content areas.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Vc78s",
                  "name": "When to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When to use\n• Interactive rows inside ListBlock (chevron variants)\n• Rows that open another view or detail (chevron variants)\n• Suggested items in generated responses (chevron variants)\n• Informational rows inside ListBlock or SectionBlock (no-chevron variants)\n• Simple text rows with optional description (no-chevron variants)\n• Compact navigation rows inside generated content\n• Clickable list entries inside a Card\n• Rows with title and optional description",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "h1cl7g",
                  "name": "When not to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When NOT to use\n• Non-interactive plain text lists — use TextContent / Stack\n• Checkbox rows — use Checkbox\n• Radio rows — use Radio\n• Tag lists — use Tag\n• Accordion sections — use Accordion / Collapse\n• Follow-up actions — use FollowUpBlock / Button\n• Large data table rows — use DataTable patterns",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "NPW7A",
                  "name": "Variants",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Variants / Defaults\n• chevron: true | false  →  true\n• description: false | true  →  false\n• hasBorder: false | true  →  false\n• state: default | hover | disabled  →  default\n• width: fill  →  fill\n\nChevron variants (interactive):\n• default — title + trailing chevron, no border\n• with-description — title + description + chevron\n• with-border — title + chevron + bottom Separator\n• with-description-border — title + description + chevron + bottom Separator\n• hover — title and chevron shift to $colors-text-header (no filled background)\n• disabled — all text and icon use $colors-text-disabled\n• long-content — wrapping title + description + chevron\n\nNo-chevron variants (informational):\n• no-chevron — title only, no trailing icon\n• no-chevron-description — title + description, no trailing icon\n• no-chevron-border — title + bottom Separator, no trailing icon\n• no-chevron-description-border — title + description + bottom Separator, no trailing icon\n\nNo-chevron rows do not reserve trailing icon space. They should not look clickable.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "g2Fy5",
                  "name": "Composition map",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Composition map\n• ListRow = row container + text Stack + optional chevron icon + optional Separator\n• One-line rows have explicit height 40px with vertical padding $spacing-2xs (8px top, 8px bottom) and no horizontal padding\n• Two-line variants (with-description, with-description-border, no-chevron-description, no-chevron-description-border, long-content) keep content-based height — not fixed to 40px\n• Chevron variants use horizontal layout with alignItems center and gap $spacing-xs\n• No-chevron variants use vertical layout with justifyContent center — same height, same left alignment, no trailing icon space\n• Border variants use a vertical wrapper with height 40px, padding-top $spacing-2xs, and justifyContent space_between — Separator is pinned to the bottom edge\n• Text Stack (vertical frame) holds title and optional description\n• Title uses $typo-primary-sm-regular-* (14 px) + $colors-text-body\n• Description uses $typo-primary-xs-regular-* (12 px) + $colors-text-meta\n• Chevron (interactive variants only) uses lucide chevron-right, 16 × 16, $colors-text-meta\n• No-chevron variants omit the chevron entirely — no hidden or disabled icon layer\n• Border variants use a real Separator component ref (full-width, padding overridden to 0)\n• No hidden placeholder layers — all internal nodes are visible and active",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "FeskS",
                  "name": "Token usage",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Token usage\n\nLayout\n• One-line row height = 40px (explicit)\n• Row vertical padding = $spacing-2xs (8px top, 8px bottom)\n• Row horizontal padding = none\n• Border variants: height 40px, padding-top only $spacing-2xs, justifyContent space_between — Separator pinned to bottom edge\n• Two-line variants: content-based height (no explicit 40px), vertical padding $spacing-2xs\n• Row gap (text ↔ chevron, chevron variants) = $spacing-xs\n• Text Stack gap (title ↔ description) = $spacing-3xs\n• No corner radius on row\n\nTitle\n• Typography = $typo-primary-sm-regular-* (14 px, weight normal)\n• Color = $colors-text-body\n\nDescription\n• Typography = $typo-primary-xs-regular-* (12 px, weight normal)\n• Color = $colors-text-meta\n\nChevron icon (chevron variants only)\n• Family = lucide, name = chevron-right\n• Size = 16 × 16\n• Color = $colors-text-meta\n\nHover state (chevron variants only)\n• No background fill\n• Title color = $colors-text-header\n• Chevron color = $colors-text-header\n\nDisabled state\n• Text = $colors-text-disabled\n• Icon = $colors-text-disabled\n\nBorder (hasBorder: true)\n• Uses Separator component ref (full-width, padding overridden to 0)\n• Separator pinned to bottom edge via justifyContent space_between\n\nNo-chevron variants\n• Same 40px height and vertical padding as chevron variants\n• No horizontal padding\n• No trailing icon, no reserved icon space\n• No hover state by default\n• Transparent background\n\nMotion\n• No motion tokens applied at the ListRow level. Transitions are handled in implementation.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "H4iLCE",
                  "name": "Resize behavior",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Resize behavior\n• Row container accepts fill_container to stretch with parent\n• Text Stack fills available width via fill_container\n• Title text uses textGrowth: fixed-width + fill_container for wrapping\n• Description text uses textGrowth: fixed-width + fill_container for wrapping\n• Chevron icon (when present) stays fixed 16 × 16 and aligned to the right\n• No-chevron rows do not reserve trailing icon space — text fills the full row width\n• Gap between text and chevron maintained by $spacing-xs (chevron variants)\n• Separator fills the full row width via fill_container\n• No overflow when compressed — text wraps, chevron (if present) stays fixed\n• No detached, fixed-width, or floating internal layers",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "aG1yj",
                  "name": "Accessibility",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Accessibility\nChevron variants represent interactive rows and should use button or link semantics with a descriptive label (the title text). They should be keyboard accessible. Hover state shifts title and chevron color for visual feedback.\n\nNo-chevron variants represent informational rows and should use semantic text or list structure, not interactive roles. They do not need keyboard focus or action handlers.\n\nDisabled state should not be focusable if implementation disables interaction. Preserve reading order: title, description, action indicator (chevron, if present).",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
