            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "KGoZK",
              "name": "SectionBlock Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 32,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "d4GN1U",
                  "name": "Docs Title",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-header",
                  "content": "SectionBlock",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "da544",
                  "name": "Docs Subtitle",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-meta",
                  "content": "Chat Section Container Organism",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "flLHo",
                  "name": "Purpose",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Purpose\nA chat-oriented section container for generated UI responses. SectionBlock groups related content under a titled Card surface, supporting text, callouts, simple lists, and collapsible content. It composes Card (surface), CardHeader (title/description), TextContent (body copy), and optionally Callout, ListRow/no-chevron (informational list rows), or Accordion into a single cohesive organism. SectionBlock does not nest other P3 organisms (e.g. ListBlock). Content is arranged with vertical flex-layout frames — no hidden placeholder layers.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Wmv72",
                  "name": "When to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When to use\n• Grouped generated response sections\n• Explanations with supporting details\n• Recommendations with supporting rationale\n• Content that needs a titled container\n• Sections that may contain lists, callouts, or accordions\n• Educational content with notes, tips, or warnings\n• Summary sections in long responses",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "PWjvy",
                  "name": "When not to use",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "When NOT to use\n• Simple structured lists — use ListBlock\n• Follow-up suggestions — use FollowUpBlock\n• Freeform prose without a container — use TextContent\n• Large data tables — use DataTable\n• Page-level layout — use PageLayout\n• Primary navigation",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "SpwJb",
                  "name": "Variants",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Variants / Defaults\n• contentType: text | callout | list | accordion  →  text\n• density: default | compact  →  default\n• description: true | false  →  true\n• width: fill  →  fill\n\nDefault variant uses Card with $spacing-md padding, CardHeader/description for title (18 px) + subtitle (16 px, text-meta), and a vertical body content stack of TextContent blocks (14 px). Body text in the default variant is overridden to $colors-text-meta; other variants use the TextContent default of $colors-text-body.\n\nWith-callout variant adds a visible Callout component (info intent) below the body text — this is a real Callout ref, not a custom border or hidden toggle.\n\nWith-list variant embeds direct ListRow/no-chevron-border and ListRow/no-chevron refs inside a listItems frame for simple informational rows. Does NOT nest ListBlock (both are P3 organisms). Rows use ListRow/no-chevron-border for all but the last row, which uses ListRow/no-chevron (no trailing separator).\n\nWith-accordion variant embeds a real Accordion component for collapsible content sections. Accordion item titles use $typo-primary-base-regular-* and $colors-text-header.\n\nCompact variant uses Card/dense with smaller padding ($spacing-sm) and CardHeader (title-only, no description). Content gap is $spacing-2xs.\n\nLong-content variant demonstrates multiple paragraphs of TextContent wrapping cleanly inside the Card.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "pZniH",
                  "name": "Composition map",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Composition map\n• SectionBlock = Card + CardHeader + TextContent + optional Callout / ListRow refs / Accordion\n• Card ref provides the outer surface (background, border, radius, padding)\n• CardHeader/description ref provides title and optional description\n• CardHeader ref (title-only) is used for compact density\n• Content frame arranges header and body content vertically\n• TextContent ref provides body copy paragraphs\n• Callout ref provides notes, tips, warnings (with-callout variant)\n• listItems frame holds ListRow/no-chevron-border and ListRow/no-chevron refs (with-list variant)\n• ListRow/no-chevron-border includes a built-in Separator — no extra Separator refs needed\n• ListRow/no-chevron is used for the final row (no trailing separator)\n• SectionBlock does NOT nest other P3 organisms (ListBlock, FollowUpBlock, etc.)\n• Accordion ref provides collapsible content sections (with-accordion variant)\n• Card/dense ref is used for compact density (smaller padding)\n• No hidden placeholder layers — all internal nodes are visible and active",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "S2TnB",
                  "name": "Token usage",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Token usage\n\nSurface\n• Card background = $colors-background-surface\n• Card border = $colors-borders-light (1 px, inside)\n• Card radius = $radius-xs\n• Card padding default = $spacing-md\n• Card padding compact = $spacing-sm (via Card/dense)\n\nSpacing\n• Content gap (header → body) = $spacing-sm\n• Content gap compact = $spacing-2xs\n• CardHeader internal gap (title ↔ description) = $spacing-3xs\n• Body content gap between paragraphs = $spacing-sm\n• List items gap = 0 (separators built into ListRow/no-chevron-border)\n\nTitle\n• Typography = $typo-primary-md-semibold-* (18 px, weight 600)\n• Color = $colors-text-header (inherited from Label via CardHeader)\n\nDescription / subtitle\n• Typography = $typo-primary-base-regular-* (16 px, weight normal)\n• Color = $colors-text-meta\n\nBody text\n• Component = TextContent ref\n• Typography = $typo-primary-sm-regular-* (14 px, weight normal)\n• Color = $colors-text-body by default (via TextContent); the default variant overrides body text to $colors-text-meta\n\nCallout (with-callout variant)\n• Uses Callout component ref (info intent: $sky-50 bg, $sky-100 border)\n\nList rows (with-list variant)\n• ListRow/no-chevron-border and ListRow/no-chevron refs\n• One-line row height = 40px (inherited from ListRow)\n• Row vertical padding = $spacing-2xs (8px top, 8px bottom), no horizontal padding\n• Title = $typo-primary-sm-regular-*, $colors-text-body\n• Border variant includes Separator pinned to bottom edge ($colors-borders-light, 1 px)\n• SectionBlock does not nest ListBlock\n\nAccordion (with-accordion variant)\n• Uses Accordion component ref\n• Item titles = $typo-primary-base-regular-*, $colors-text-header\n• Open item body = $typo-primary-sm-regular-*\n\nMotion\n• No motion tokens applied at the SectionBlock level. Child component transitions are inherited.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "VtG1H",
                  "name": "Resize behavior",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Resize behavior\n• Outer wrapper frame accepts fill_container to stretch with parent\n• Card fills the wrapper width via fill_container\n• CardHeader fills Card content area via fill_container\n• Content frame fills Card content area via fill_container\n• TextContent body text uses textGrowth: fixed-width + fill_container for wrapping\n• Callout fills the available width via fill_container\n• ListRow/no-chevron refs fill available width via fill_container\n• Accordion fills the available width via fill_container\n• No overflow when compressed — all internal layers stretch/shrink with parent\n• No detached, fixed-width, or floating internal layers",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "w8i6t9",
                  "name": "Accessibility",
                  "fill": "$sem-text-body",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Accessibility\nSectionBlock should expose a clear section label via role=\"region\" and aria-labelledby referencing the CardHeader title. Preserve logical reading order: title, description, body content, nested content (callout, list rows, accordion). List rows use ListRow/no-chevron refs and should use semantic list elements (ul). Accordion content must remain keyboard accessible. Avoid invalid nested interactive semantics. CardHeader title provides the accessible name for the section.",
                  "lineHeight": "$line-height-sm",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
                  "fontSize": "$text-size-sm",
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "NFuGX",
          "name": "SectionBlock Demo Examples Title",
          "fill": "$sem-text-header",
          "content": "SectionBlock — Demo Examples",
          "lineHeight": "$line-height-xl",
          "fontFamily": "$font-primary",
          "fontSize": "$text-size-xl",
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "n5z1IN",
          "name": "SectionBlock Demos Row",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "gap": "$spacing-xl",
          "children": [
