              "name": "TreemapChart Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 32,
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "p3Ez9d",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "TreemapChart",
                      "fontSize": "$text-size-lg",
                      "fontWeight": "700",
                      "lineHeight": 1.3333
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "DtTUl",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "A treemap chart organism showing part-to-whole allocation with nested rectangular cells. Each cell's area is proportional to its percentage of the total. Built on Card with CardHeader and a clipped treemap area using flexbox layout."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "nMPqa",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "When to use",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p98oL",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Use for asset allocation views, portfolio breakdowns, or any part-to-whole composition where you want to show relative sizes. Use with-values when dollar amounts supplement percentages. Use compact in dense dashboards. Use no-card when embedding inside another container."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "iyRpX",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "When not to use",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "rqDnV",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Do not use for time-series data — use AreaChart or BarChart. Do not use for comparisons between separate groups — use grouped BarChart. Do not use when there are more than 8 categories — small cells become unreadable. For simple breakdowns with 2–3 items, a DonutChart may be clearer."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "E2ojU",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Variants",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "DaLsB",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "default: Card wrapper with header, 5 cells showing asset name and percentage. Large left cell for the dominant allocation, right column subdivided.\nwith-values: Same layout plus dollar amounts below percentages on larger cells.\nwith-tooltip: Same layout as default with a ChartTooltip overlay showing details for a selected cell. Tooltip displays category name header, allocation percentage, and monetary value. Used when small cells cannot fit all details inline.\ncompact: 360px width, 180px map height, smaller typography (xs/base instead of sm/lg).\nno-card: Header + treemap without Card wrapper, for embedding in other containers."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "N6RFm",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Composition",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "v9UsFP",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "TreemapChart = Card + CardHeader + treemapArea (frame, horizontal, clip:true, cornerRadius $radius-3xs) + optional ChartTooltip. Treemap area uses nested flexbox: left cell (fixed width) + right column (fill_container, vertical) containing top cells and a bottom horizontal row. Each cell is a frame with categorical fill, padding, name text, and percentage text. The with-tooltip variant adds a ChartTooltip/multi-series instance inside chartContent with absolute positioning."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "hL4wY",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Token usage",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cpROM",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Cell fills: $chart-categorical/color-01 through color-05. Dark cells (color-01 purple, color-03 indigo, color-04 blue, color-05 teal): $colors-text-reverse for text. Light cells (color-02 cyan): $colors-text-header for WCAG contrast. Names: $typo-primary-sm-regular (default), $typo-primary-xs-regular (compact/small cells). Percentages: $typo-primary-lg-semibold (default), $typo-primary-base-semibold (compact). Gap between cells: 2px. Tooltip marker matches the selected cell color using the same $chart-categorical token. Tooltip uses ChartTooltip component tokens for background, border, and shadow. Monetary values in the tooltip use MoneyText where supported; percentages do not use MoneyText."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "Pggnh",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Resize behavior",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "wMVv7",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Card fills available width. Treemap area uses fill_container width. The dominant cell has a fixed pixel width proportional to its percentage; right column fills the remainder. Inner cells use fixed heights with the bottom row using fill_container. Cell dimensions should be recalculated when the container width changes."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "ZbUxH",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Accessibility",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "BtB6m",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Text on dark cells (color-01, color-03, color-05) uses $colors-text-reverse (white) with contrast ratios above 4.5:1. Text on the cyan cell (color-02) uses $colors-text-header (dark) for 4.67:1 contrast. Text on the blue cell (color-04) uses white at 3.68:1 — passes WCAG AA for large/bold text. Each cell has both a text label and a percentage value, so color is never the sole identifier."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "oDfER",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
