            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "qXMuh",
              "name": "SankeyDiagram Documentation",
              "width": 640,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 32,
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "nU5iW",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "SankeyDiagram",
                      "fontSize": "$text-size-lg",
                      "fontWeight": "700",
                      "lineHeight": 1.3333
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "GpGN2",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "A Sankey flow diagram organism showing how values flow from source categories through intermediate nodes to destination categories. Three columns of colored node bars connected by curved bezier flow bands. Built on Card with CardHeader/description."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "uiubG",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "When to use",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "VT9mz",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Use for income-to-expense flow visualization, portfolio allocation tracking, or any data that flows from sources through intermediate stages to destinations. Use with-values when dollar amounts should supplement labels. Use compact in dense dashboards. Use no-card when embedding inside another container."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "XMAF4",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "When not to use",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "mGPzB",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Do not use for time-series data — use AreaChart. Do not use for simple part-to-whole — use DonutChart or TreemapChart. Do not use for comparisons between groups — use BarChart. Not suitable when there are fewer than 3 source or destination nodes."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "mC6h0",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Variants",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "qbcOF",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "default: Card wrapper with CardHeader/description, 3-column Sankey with source (4 nodes), intermediate (4 nodes), and destination (7 nodes) connected by flow bands.\ncompact: 360px width, proportionally scaled node heights and positions.\nwith-values: Same as default plus MoneyText/sm amounts next to each source and destination node label.\nwith-tooltip: Same as default with a ChartTooltip overlay showing details for a selected flow. Tooltip displays source → destination header, monetary amount, and share percentage. Used when flow values and relationships are hard to read from geometry alone.\nno-card: CardHeader + Sankey plot without Card wrapper, for embedding in other containers."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "zkUiE",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Composition",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "MArA3",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "SankeyDiagram = Card + CardHeader/description + plotArea (frame, layout:none, clip:true) + optional MoneyText values + optional ChartTooltip. Each node is a rectangle (12px wide, 10px compact) with categorical fill and $radius-3xs cornerRadius. Each label is a Tag atom instance with the node's $chart-categorical color as fill background — white text ($base-white) on dark fills (color-01 through color-05), dark text ($colors-text-header) on light fills (color-06, color-07). Compact variant overrides Tag padding to $spacing-3xs and uses $typo-primary-2xs-regular typography. In with-values, each source and intermediate node uses a vertical frame group containing a MoneyText/sm instance above and a Tag instance below, centered near the node bar. Flow bands are individual SVG path nodes using bezier curves (M/c/l/c/z) with the source node's color at opacity:0.3. The with-tooltip variant adds a ChartTooltip/multi-series instance inside chartContent with absolute positioning. Real dynamic label placement is implementation-level."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "dmHbo",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Token usage",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "nAk8z",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Node fills: $chart-categorical/color-01 through color-07, cornerRadius: $radius-3xs. Flow bands: same token colors at opacity:0.3. Label tags: Tag atom instances with $chart-categorical/color-01–07 fills matching each node. Text: $base-white on dark fills (01–05), $colors-text-header on light fills (06–07). Compact variant: Tag padding overridden to $spacing-3xs, label text uses $typo-primary-2xs-regular. MoneyText/sm for with-values variant amounts positioned above Tag labels in vertical frame groups to avoid flow band overlap. Tooltip marker matches selected flow/source token using the same $chart-categorical color. Tooltip uses ChartTooltip component tokens for background, border, and shadow. Monetary values in the tooltip use MoneyText where supported; percentages do not use MoneyText. Card uses $colors-background-surface, $colors-borders-light."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "THHno",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Resize behavior",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "kxXLv",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "Card fills available width. The plotArea uses fill_container width with layout:none. Node positions and band geometry are computed relative to plotArea dimensions. Compact variant uses a scale factor (sy=ph/280) to proportionally resize all coordinates."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "TumHO",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Accessibility",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "KORzg",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "All node bars have paired Tag labels with white text on dark categorical fills (color-01 through color-05) or dark text ($colors-text-header) on light categorical fills (color-06, color-07), maintaining WCAG AA contrast. Flow bands are decorative (opacity:0.3) and do not convey information independently — each band connects labeled nodes. Color is never the sole identifier of a data point."
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "F5ecpM",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "H9ao5i",
                  "descendants": {
                    "nZEDL": {
                      "content": "Implementation note",
                      "fontWeight": "600"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "m6pGu",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "i5vQ3i",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "FHA10": {
                      "content": "This is a visual chart component. Node positions, band geometry, and MoneyText values are static representations. Dynamic data binding, hover states, animation, and tooltip display are implementation concerns. Flow band geometry uses SVG bezier paths computed from source and destination node positions. The with-tooltip variant shows how ChartTooltip surfaces flow detail for selected bands; real hover/focus behavior is implementation-level."
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
